# A.R.I.D. Web Dashboard Rules

The dashboard is an LGU/health-worker monitoring tool. It expects an internet connection.

1. Never write classification, GPS, risk level, points, or syncStatus. Those are produced only by the mobile app.
2. The only allowed dashboard write is the lightweight `reviewStatus` / `reviewedAt` / `reviewedBy` fields on an existing report.
3. Only display reports that are already in Firestore (synced). Never invent or recompute risk levels.
4. Use Firestore `onSnapshot` listeners for live updates — no manual refresh as the primary data path.
5. Same color tokens as mobile (`#4A7A8C`, `#6B9080`, risk red/yellow/green). Risk colors are for markers, badges, and hotspot fills only.
6. Keep this a monitoring complement to the mobile app, not a second capture/classification app.
7. Report photos are Cloudinary URLs on Firestore documents. Do not add Firebase Storage.
